  "contract_review": {
    "external_policy": "palette_policy retains own empty/exact allowlist and whole-PNG requirements. pixel_policy has only empty/rgba; both nonempty refuse before selection. Report palette_policy remains profile-derived, pixel_policy only appears when explicit. Unknown/wrong-field/case/conflict/missing-color-policy refusals independently exercised.",
    "codec_policy": "Only empty/exact/rgba accepted. rgba requires depth32 after the unchanged finite512square/version0/RF0504/TEX0/paletteBase/storage/footprint checks; exact remains whole standard8 only. No other direct mode enabled.",
    "default_refusals": "Default source and candidate monochrome checks remain. Sourcealpha>128 is an unconditional direct guard, including rgba. The old combined font-source message is split into native-alpha and monochrome diagnostics; the meaningful refusals remain. Explicit rgba intentionally permits color only.",
    "raw_bytes": "One existing direct walk reads/writes independent R/G/B channels, retains hidden RGB atalpha0 and applies the existing (A+1)/2 native-alpha rounding/ties-up rule. It reencodes only pixels that differ, retains clone-only writes and nil partial results on refusal. No palette normalization/transparent-RGB cleanup/premultiplication added to direct mode.",
    "masks": "Existing rectangle validation and pre-quantization changed-pixel refusal stay intact. A candidate outside the mask must refuse even if it would round to the same native byte; independently verified outside refusal and inside success as exact no-op.",
    "reuse": "Existing parser/native mode guard/pixel walk/alpha expression/clone/mask/readInput/run/writeNewFile owners remain. No duplicated quantizer or conversion engine. Existing CLI fixture facts now read from canonical texture testdata instead of a copied three-row table.",
    "load": "Single bounded artifact CLI; existing512square direct loop and caps unchanged, no new global state or publication path."
  },
